The /welcome login page is rendered by the SignInUp page component. Here's how it's wired:

  Route path
  - packages/twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts:5: SignInUp = '/welcome'

  Page component
  - packages/twenty-front/src/pages/auth/SignInUp.tsx: the login/sign-up page itself.

  Router registration (loaded lazily as ~/pages/auth/SignInUp)
  - packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/hooks/useCreateRootAppRouter.tsx:38: the root domain. Line 69 also redirects other paths to /welcome.
  - packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/hooks/useCreateWorkspaceAppRouter.tsx:231: the workspace subdomain.

  Where the page's content lives
  - packages/twenty-front/src/modules/auth/sign-in-up/components/: the sub-components, such as SignInUpStandardContent.tsx and the step components under internal/.
  - packages/twenty-front/src/modules/auth/sign-in-up/hooks/useSignInUp.ts: the form logic.
  - packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/layout/page/components/AuthFlowLayout.tsx: the surrounding layout.

  SignInUp.tsx was modified on Sep 16, more recently than the other auth pages, so it may already have changes on your feat-rebrand branch.
